title: 'frame-support: implement transaction chain batching via event field capture'
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    Adds opt-in chain batch capture to FRAME pallet events.

    ## New attributes

    Pallets can annotate their event enum with `#[pallet::capture_for_chain_batch]` and
    mark individual named variant fields with `#[chain_batch(capture = "name")]`. When
    `deposit_event` is called, the macro-generated implementation will SCALE-encode those
    fields and push them into the dispatch context alongside the normal event deposit. Any
    code running in the same dispatch can then retrieve and consume the captured data via
    `frame_support::dispatch_context::get_captured_event_fields()`.

    ```rust
    #[pallet::event]
    #[pallet::generate_deposit(pub fn deposit_event)]
    #[pallet::capture_for_chain_batch]
    pub enum Event<T: Config> {
        Transfer {
            #[chain_batch(capture = "amount")]
            amount: T::Balance,
            #[chain_batch(capture = "from")]
            from: T::AccountId,
            to: T::AccountId, // not captured
        },
    }
    ```

    ## New runtime API (`frame-support`)

    - `dispatch_context::capture_event_field(pallet, variant, field_name, encoded_bytes)` —
      called automatically by the generated `deposit_event`; no-op outside a dispatch context.
    - `dispatch_context::get_captured_event_fields() -> Option<Vec<CapturedEventEntry>>` —
      drains all captured entries for the current dispatch; returns `None` outside a context.
    - `dispatch_context::CapturedEventEntry` — public struct carrying `pallet`, `variant`,
      `field_name`, and the raw SCALE-encoded `value`.

    ## Fixes applied to the original implementation

    The original commit left the feature entirely non-functional. The following bugs were
    found and fixed before any pallet could successfully compile with the new attributes:

    - `capture_event_field` and `get_captured_event_fields` did not exist; added them.
    - `#[pallet::capture_for_chain_batch]` was not stripped from the event enum's attribute
      list, causing an "unknown attribute" compile error in every consumer crate.
    - `#[chain_batch(capture = "...")]` was not stripped from variant field attributes,
      causing `Encode`, `Decode`, and `TypeInfo` derive macros to reject the unknown attribute.
    - `maybe_allow_attrs` was not forwarded to the capture code path, silently dropping
      compiler-warning suppression on adopting pallets.
    - `.encode()` was called as a method, requiring `Encode` to be in scope in generated
      code where it is not; replaced with UFCS `Encode::encode(field)`.
    - Local variables (`event_use_gen`, `type_impl_gen`, etc.) were computed before the
      capture/normal branch, making them dead code in the capture path.
    - `HashMap` was used to group variant fields, producing non-deterministic token order
      across compilations; replaced with `BTreeMap` for reproducible macro output.
crates:
- name: frame-support
  bump: minor
- name: frame-support-procedural
  bump: minor
